IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sgb1-s148-bankrupt-unfit`

-- Tests for sgb1-s148-bankrupt-unfit.l4 (Companies Act 1967, ss 148, 149, 149A; text lines 11925-12234 of CoA1967.txt).
-- Every expected value was written from the text of the Act, not from what the code printed; each group names the words it rests on.
-- JUST TRUE yes; JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words; NOTHING the text does not say.


-- s 148(1): "Every person who, being an undischarged bankrupt ..., acts as director of, or ... takes part in ... the management of, any corporation, except with the permission of the Court or the written permission of the Official Assignee, shall be guilty of an offence"
-- bankrupt, acting, no permission
#ASSERT `s 148(1) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the permission of the Court
#ASSERT `s 148(1) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the written permission of the Official Assignee
#ASSERT `s 148(1) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not an undischarged bankrupt
#ASSERT `s 148(1) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not acting as director or in the management
#ASSERT `s 148(1) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- section 4(7): a reference to an undischarged bankrupt covers an undischarged bankrupt or insolvent under a written law, unless a contrary intention appears
#ASSERT `s 148(1) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years or both
#ASSERT `s 148(1) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`s 148(1) penalty` OF 10000, 24, TRUE)
-- the text states a penalty only for a guilty person
#ASSERT `s 148(1) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 148(2): "the Court or the Official Assignee may refuse the application or approve the application subject to such condition"
#ASSERT `s 148(2) the Court or the Official Assignee may refuse the application or approve it subject to conditions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a "may" gated by "On an application by an undischarged bankrupt under subsection (1)": group 3, ruling (b)
#ASSERT `s 148(2) the Court or the Official Assignee may refuse the application or approve it subject to conditions` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 148(3): "The Court must not give permission under this section unless notice ... has been served on the Minister and on the Official Assignee and the Minister and the Official Assignee or either of them may be represented"
-- both conditions of the unless are met
#ASSERT `s 148(3) the subsection bars the Court from giving permission` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the second condition is missing
#ASSERT `s 148(3) the subsection bars the Court from giving permission` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the first condition is missing
#ASSERT `s 148(3) the subsection bars the Court from giving permission` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 148(4): "within 14 days after the issue of the Court order or written permission, lodge a copy"; issued 1 June 2026, 14 days after is 15 June 2026
#ASSERT `s 148(4) the last day for lodging the copy of the order or written permission` (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS (Date 15 6 2026)
-- on the fourteenth day
#ASSERT `s 148(4) the person has lodged the copy within the time the subsection allows` TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a day late
#ASSERT `s 148(4) the person has lodged the copy within the time the subsection allows` TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 16 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- early
#ASSERT `s 148(4) the person has lodged the copy within the time the subsection allows` TRUE (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 2 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no permission was granted: outside "Any person who has been granted permission"
#ASSERT `s 148(4) the person has lodged the copy within the time the subsection allows` FALSE (Date 1 6 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 149(5)(a): a company has gone into liquidation (i) if wound up by the Court, on the date of the filing of the winding up application; (ii) where a provisional liquidator was appointed, at the time when the declaration was lodged with the Registrar; (iii) in any other case, on the date of the passing of the resolution for the voluntary winding up
#ASSERT `s 149(5)(a) the date on which the company has gone into liquidation` `s 149(5)(a)(i) it was wound up by the Court` (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 2 3 2020) (Date 3 3 2020) EQUALS (Date 1 3 2020)
#ASSERT `s 149(5)(a) the date on which the company has gone into liquidation` `s 149(5)(a)(ii) a provisional liquidator was appointed under section 161(1) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 2 3 2020) (Date 3 3 2020) EQUALS (Date 2 3 2020)
#ASSERT `s 149(5)(a) the date on which the company has gone into liquidation` `s 149(5)(a)(iii) any other case` (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 2 3 2020) (Date 3 3 2020) EQUALS (Date 3 3 2020)

-- s 149(5)(b): "a company was insolvent at the time it has gone into liquidation if it was unable to pay its debts"
#ASSERT `s 149(5)(b) the company was insolvent at the time it went into liquidation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a condition introduced with "if" that fails
#ASSERT `s 149(5)(b) the company was insolvent at the time it went into liquidation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 149(5), closing words: references to a person's conduct as a director "include, where any of those companies have become insolvent, references to that person's conduct in relation to any matter connected with or arising out of the insolvency"
#ASSERT `s 149(5) the person's conduct as a director of the company includes the conduct in relation to a matter connected with the insolvency` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the company has not become insolvent: outside the "where" of the inclusion, and "include" leaves the list open
#ASSERT `s 149(5) the person's conduct as a director of the company includes the conduct in relation to a matter connected with the insolvency` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- conduct not connected with the insolvency: "include" leaves the list open
#ASSERT `s 149(5) the person's conduct as a director of the company includes the conduct in relation to a matter connected with the insolvency` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 149(10): "This section does not apply unless the company ... has gone into insolvent liquidation on or after 15 August 1984 and the conduct to which the Court is to have regard does not include conduct as a director of a company that has gone into liquidation before that date"
-- on the day itself
#ASSERT `s 149(10) the section applies to the company's liquidation` (Date 15 8 1984) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the day before
#ASSERT `s 149(10) the section applies to the company's liquidation` (Date 14 8 1984) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- liquidation before that date: that conduct is not included
#ASSERT `s 149(10) the conduct as a director of the company is conduct to which the Court is to have regard` (Date 14 8 1984) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- on that date: the subsection says nothing more about the conduct
#ASSERT `s 149(10) the conduct as a director of the company is conduct to which the Court is to have regard` (Date 15 8 1984) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 149(2)(b)(i): "he or she is or has been a director of a company which has at any time gone into liquidation (whether while he or she was a director or within 3 years of his or her ceasing to be a director) and was insolvent at that time"
-- still a director when the company went into liquidation
#ASSERT `s 149(2)(b)(i) the person is or has been a director of a company that went into liquidation and was insolvent at that time` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2010) (Date 1 6 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- ceased 1 June 2017, liquidation on 1 June 2020: within 3 years
#ASSERT `s 149(2)(b)(i) the person is or has been a director of a company that went into liquidation and was insolvent at that time` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 6 2017) (Date 1 6 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a day more than 3 years after ceasing to be a director
#ASSERT `s 149(2)(b)(i) the person is or has been a director of a company that went into liquidation and was insolvent at that time` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 6 2017) (Date 2 6 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the company was not insolvent
#ASSERT `s 149(2)(b)(i) the person is or has been a director of a company that went into liquidation and was insolvent at that time` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2010) (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- never a director
#ASSERT `s 149(2)(b)(i) the person is or has been a director of a company that went into liquidation and was insolvent at that time` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 6 2017) (Date 1 6 2020) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 149(2): "The Court must make a disqualification order ... if it is satisfied that (a) ... not less than 14 days' notice ...; and (b) ... (i) ... and (ii) ... unfit"; and s 149(10)
-- exactly 14 days' notice, all else satisfied
#ASSERT `s 149(2) the Court must make a disqualification order against the person` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2010) (Date 1 6 2020) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 13 days' notice
#ASSERT `s 149(2) the Court must make a disqualification order against the person` (Date 2 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2010) (Date 1 6 2020) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the Court is not satisfied that the conduct makes the person unfit
#ASSERT `s 149(2) the Court must make a disqualification order against the person` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2010) (Date 1 6 2020) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not insolvent
#ASSERT `s 149(2) the Court must make a disqualification order against the person` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2010) (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- section 149(10): liquidation before 15 August 1984
#ASSERT `s 149(2) the Court must make a disqualification order against the person` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2010) (Date 14 8 1984) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- liquidation on 15 August 1984
#ASSERT `s 149(2) the Court must make a disqualification order against the person` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2010) (Date 15 8 1984) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 149(1): the Court may, on the application of the Minister or the Official Receiver and on being satisfied, disqualify for a period not exceeding 5 years
#ASSERT `s 149(1) the Court may make an order disqualifying the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a "may" gated by "on the application": group 3, ruling (b)
#ASSERT `s 149(1) the Court may make an order disqualifying the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a "may" gated by "on being satisfied": group 3, ruling (b)
#ASSERT `s 149(1) the Court may make an order disqualifying the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- five years is "not exceeding 5 years"
#ASSERT `s 149(1) the period the order specifies is within the limit the subsection allows` 5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 149(1) the period the order specifies is within the limit the subsection allows` 6 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 149(1) the period the order specifies is within the limit the subsection allows` 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 149(3): "If ... it appears to the Official Receiver or to the liquidator ... that the conditions mentioned in subsection (2)(b) are satisfied ... must immediately report the matter to the Minister"
#ASSERT `s 149(3) the Official Receiver or the liquidator must immediately report the matter to the Minister` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- it does not appear that the conditions are satisfied
#ASSERT `s 149(3) the Official Receiver or the liquidator must immediately report the matter to the Minister` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a director or former director of a company being wound up
#ASSERT `s 149(3) the Official Receiver or the liquidator must immediately report the matter to the Minister` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 149(4): "if default is made in complying with that requirement the Court may, on the application of the Minister, make an order"
#ASSERT `s 149(4) the Court may order the person to make good the default` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 149(4) the Court may order the person to make good the default` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 149(4) the Court may order the person to make good the default` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 149(6): the matters the Court must have regard to; the Minister may add by notification (subsection (7))
#ASSERT `s 149(6) the Court must have regard to the matter` `s 149(6)(a)(i) whether there has been any misfeasance or breach of any fiduciary or other duty by the director in relation to the company` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the last matter listed
#ASSERT `s 149(6) the Court must have regard to the matter` `s 149(6)(b)(iv) whether the causes of the company becoming insolvent are attributable to its carrying on business in a particular industry where the risk of insolvency is generally recognised to be higher` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a matter the Minister added by notification under subsection (7)
#ASSERT `s 149(6) the Court must have regard to the matter` `s 149(6) some other matter` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a matter not listed and not added: silent
#ASSERT `s 149(6) the Court must have regard to the matter` `s 149(6) some other matter` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "even though the director has not been convicted or may be criminally liable"
#ASSERT `s 149(6) the matter counts although the director has not been convicted` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 149(6) the matter counts although the director has not been convicted` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 149(7) the Minister may add to, vary or amend the matters referred to in subsection (6)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the text names notification in the Gazette
#ASSERT `s 149(7) the Minister may add to, vary or amend the matters referred to in subsection (6)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 149(8): "company" includes a corporation and a foreign company but does not include a partnership or association to which Division 1 of Part 10 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 applies
#ASSERT `s 149(8) the body is a company for the purposes of the section` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a partnership or association excluded in so many words
#ASSERT `s 149(8) the body is a company for the purposes of the section` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "includes": the list is open
#ASSERT `s 149(8) the body is a company for the purposes of the section` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 149(9): "In the case of a person who is or has been a director of a company which has gone into liquidation and is being wound up by the Court, an application ... is to be made by the Official Receiver but in any other case ... by the Minister"
#ASSERT `s 149(9) who makes the application under the section` TRUE EQUALS `s 149(9) the Official Receiver`
#ASSERT `s 149(9) who makes the application under the section` FALSE EQUALS `s 149(9) the Minister`

-- s 149(9A): "On a hearing of an application under this section (a) the Minister or the Official Receiver ... must appear ...; (b) the person against whom an order is sought may appear"
#ASSERT `s 149(9A)(a) the Minister or the Official Receiver must appear and call the attention of the Court to any relevant matter` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an "On" gate fails (ruling (c) of 2026-11-05: when and upon count as where)
#ASSERT `s 149(9A)(a) the Minister or the Official Receiver must appear and call the attention of the Court to any relevant matter` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 149(9A)(b) the person against whom an order is sought may appear and give evidence or call witnesses` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a "may" gated by "On a hearing": group 3
#ASSERT `s 149(9A)(b) the person against whom an order is sought may appear and give evidence or call witnesses` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 149(11): "A person who acts as judicial manager, receiver or receiver manager shall not be liable to have a disqualification order made against the person in respect of acts done in the person's capacity as judicial manager, receiver or receiver manager"
-- a flat negative
#ASSERT `s 149(11) the person is liable to have a disqualification order made against the person in respect of the acts` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a judicial manager, receiver or receiver manager: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 149(11) the person is liable to have a disqualification order made against the person in respect of the acts` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- acts not done in that capacity: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 149(11) the person is liable to have a disqualification order made against the person in respect of the acts` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 149(12): "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years or to both"
#ASSERT `s 149(12) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 149(12) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 149(12) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST (`s 149(12) penalty` OF 10000, 24, TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 149(12) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 149(13): "Nothing in this section prevents a person who is disqualified ... from applying for permission of the Court"
#ASSERT `s 149(13) the person may apply to the Court for permission to be concerned in or take part in the management of a company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a person not disqualified: outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 149(13) the person may apply to the Court for permission to be concerned in or take part in the management of a company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 149(14): "On the hearing of an application made under subsection (13) or (15), the Minister or the Official Receiver must appear"
#ASSERT `s 149(14) the Minister or the Official Receiver must appear and call the attention of the Court to any matter relevant to the application` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an "On" gate that fails
#ASSERT `s 149(14) the Minister or the Official Receiver must appear and call the attention of the Court to any matter relevant to the application` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 149A(1): "where a company is ordered to be wound up ... on the ground that it is being used for purposes against national security or interest, the Court may, on the application of the Minister, ... disqualify ... for a period of 3 years from the date of the making of the winding up order"
#ASSERT `s 149A(1) the Court may make an order disqualifying the person` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no application by the Minister: a "may" gated by "on the application" (group 3)
#ASSERT `s 149A(1) the Court may make an order disqualifying the person` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a "where" gate that fails
#ASSERT `s 149A(1) the Court may make an order disqualifying the person` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a director of that company
#ASSERT `s 149A(1) the Court may make an order disqualifying the person` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 3 years from the date of the winding up order
#ASSERT `s 149A(1) the last day of the disqualification` (Date 1 6 2026) EQUALS (Date 1 6 2029)

-- s 149A(2): "must not make a disqualification order ... unless the Court is satisfied that the person ... has been given not less than 14 days' notice"
-- 14 days: the unless is met
#ASSERT `s 149A(2) the subsection bars the Court from making a disqualification order against the person` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 13 days: barred
#ASSERT `s 149A(2) the subsection bars the Court from making a disqualification order against the person` (Date 2 1 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- s 149A(3): "must not make a disqualification order ... if such person proves ... that (a) ... without his or her consent or connivance; and (b) ... such diligence"
#ASSERT `s 149A(3) the subsection bars the Court from making a disqualification order against the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- only both limbs bar; otherwise the subsection is silent
#ASSERT `s 149A(3) the subsection bars the Court from making a disqualification order against the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 149A(3) the subsection bars the Court from making a disqualification order against the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 149A(4): a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years or both; (5): "foreign company" means a foreign company to which Division 2 of Part 11 applies
#ASSERT `s 149A(4) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 149A(4) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 149A(4) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST (`s 149A(4) penalty` OF 10000, 24, TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 149A(4) the most the person may be penalised on conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 149A(5) "foreign company" the body is a foreign company for the purposes of the section` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "means" definition
#ASSERT `s 149A(5) "foreign company" the body is a foreign company for the purposes of the section` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Regulative rules: each #TRACE has an EXPECT line above it naming the outcome the text gives; each rule has a breach trace where the text allows one.

-- the forbidden act occurs
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 148(1) an undischarged bankrupt must not act as director without permission` "B" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "B" DOES `s 148(1) act as director of, or take part in the management of, a corporation without the permission of the Court or the written permission of the Official Assignee` AT 4

-- nothing happens
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 148(1) an undischarged bankrupt must not act as director without permission` "B" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 4

-- on the fourteenth day after the issue
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 148(4) a person granted permission must lodge a copy within 14 days` "P" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "P" DOES `s 148(4) lodge a copy of the Court order or written permission with the Registrar` AT 14

-- a day late
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 148(4) a person granted permission must lodge a copy within 14 days` "P" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "P" DOES `s 148(4) lodge a copy of the Court order or written permission with the Registrar` AT 15

-- nothing lodged by day 15
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 148(4) a person granted permission must lodge a copy within 14 days` "P" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 15

-- an early lodging (fork P2) complies: "within 14 days"
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 148(4) a person granted permission must lodge a copy within 14 days` "P" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "P" DOES `s 148(4) lodge a copy of the Court order or written permission with the Registrar` AT 2

-- the forbidden act occurs
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 149(12) a person disqualified by an order must not act in contravention of it` "P" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "P" DOES `s 149(12) act in contravention of a disqualification order` AT 6

-- nothing happens
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 149(12) a person disqualified by an order must not act in contravention of it` "P" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 6

-- the forbidden act occurs
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 149A(4) a person disqualified by an order must not act in contravention of it` "P" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "P" DOES `s 149A(4) act in contravention of a disqualification order` AT 6

-- nothing happens
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 149A(4) a person disqualified by an order must not act in contravention of it` "P" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 6
